5	## Established facts
6	
7	- For d=3g-3+n, Poincare duality identifies W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n};Q) with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n};Q)(d). [evidence: source; FND-0001, mechanically verified for all cases.]
8	- For (g,n)=(6,6), d=21 and the ordinary cohomological degree corresponding to the Borel-Moore target is 26. [evidence: mechanical; Direct substitution gives d=3·6-3+6=21 and 2d-16=26.]
9	- With W_f=(O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*O_{P1}(-f))|_C, one has deg(W_f|_C)=4g+12-4f. [evidence: source; SRC-0004, Lemma 10.6 degree calculation, including the negative sign in gamma^*O(-f).]
10	- For g=6 and f=5, deg(W_5)=16 and deg(W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1})=6. [evidence: mechanical; Substitution into deg(W_f)=4g+12-4f gives 16, followed by 16-deg(omega_C)=16-10=6.]
11	- For a marked divisor Gamma of degree six, deg(omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma))=0, whereas deg(omega_C tensor W_4^vee(Gamma))=-4. [evidence: mechanical; Using 4f+n-2g-14 gives 20+6-12-14=0 for f=5 and 16+6-12-14=-4 for f=4.]
12	- The f=4 obstruction space H^0(C,omega_C tensor W_4^vee(Gamma)) vanishes. [evidence: mechanical; Its defining line bundle has degree -4, and a line bundle of negative degree on a smooth projective curve has no nonzero global section.]
13	- For the f=5 summand, H^0(C,omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma)) is nonzero exactly when O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}. [evidence: mechanical; The obstruction line bundle has degree zero; a degree-zero line bundle on a smooth projective curve has a nonzero section exactly when it is trivial.]
14	- The degree 26 target equals the virtual cohomological dimension for M_{6,6}, so vanishing strictly above virtual cohomological dimension does not settle it. [evidence: source; FND-0035 explicitly places (6,6) at virtual cohomological dimension.]
15	- For M_{6,6} to M_{6,5}, the q=0 term H^{26}(M_{6,5};Q) vanishes, and no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26 when fibre cohomology is confined to q=0,1. [evidence: source; FND-0036, mechanically verified for degree 26.]
16	- The reduced-distinct-support locus in a degree-six relative linear system is open, and ordering its six support points gives a finite etale S_6-cover. [evidence: source; The canonical geometric bottleneck explicitly specifies the reduced-support open and its finite etale S_6-cover.]
17	
18	## Candidate ideas requiring proof
19	
20	- Identify W_5 with omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D) for a divisor D in a balanced tetragonal g^1_4, thereby interpreting the marked divisor as residual to D in a canonical divisor.
21	- Construct the rank-drop locus over the moduli of balanced tetragonal structures as the reduced-support open of the relative linear system |W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}|, followed by the finite etale ordering cover.
22	- Stratify the relative degree-six linear system by h^0(W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}) and determine every stratum's components, dimensions, stabilizers, and map to tetragonal moduli.
23	- For a free tetragonal pencil D with h^0(O_C(D))=2, Riemann-Roch suggests h^0(omega_C(-D))=3 and hence a P^2-family of residual degree-six divisors.
24	- Use localization and Gysin maps to isolate the exact contributions of the rank-drop locus to Gr^W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q).
25	- Reduce the lowest-weight cohomology of all relevant strata and coefficient systems to explicitly controlled configuration or Hurwitz spaces.
26	- Prove that every exact codimension-13 contribution supported on the rank-drop locus is a sum of Q(-13).
27	
28	## Mathematical constraints
29	
30	- M_{0,b} has cohomology only in even degrees. [reason: Already M_{0,4} is P^1 minus three points and has nonzero H^1; mixed-Tate cohomology does not imply concentration in even degrees.]
31	- An arbitrary finite etale cover of a space with pure-Tate cohomology also has pure-Tate cohomology. [reason: Transfer makes the base cohomology a direct summand of the cover's cohomology, not conversely; the cover may acquire additional non-Tate summands.]
32	- Being finite over an open subset of M_{0,b} is sufficient to make every lowest-weight cohomology group of a Hurwitz space Tate. [reason: Finiteness alone gives no such control on the new cohomology or monodromy of the covering space.]
33	- The h^0-stratification of a degree-six line bundle L with chi(L)=1 can contain an r=0 stratum. [reason: Riemann-Roch gives h^0(L)-h^1(L)=1, hence h^0(L)=1+h^1(L) is at least one.]
