- For a marked divisor Gamma of degree six, deg(omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma))=0, whereas deg(omega_C tensor W_4^vee(Gamma))=-4. [evidence: mechanical; Using 4f+n-2g-14 gives 20+6-12-14=0 for f=5 and 16+6-12-14=-4 for f=4.]
- The f=4 obstruction space H^0(C,omega_C tensor W_4^vee(Gamma)) vanishes. [evidence: mechanical; Its defining line bundle has degree -4, and a line bundle of negative degree on a smooth projective curve has no nonzero global section.]
- For the f=5 summand, H^0(C,omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma)) is nonzero exactly when O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}. [evidence: mechanical; The obstruction line bundle has degree zero; a degree-zero line bundle on a smooth projective curve has a nonzero section exactly when it is trivial.]
- The degree 26 target equals the virtual cohomological dimension for M_{6,6}, so vanishing strictly above virtual cohomological dimension does not settle it. [evidence: source; FND-0035 explicitly places (6,6) at virtual cohomological dimension.]
- For M_{6,6} to M_{6,5}, the q=0 term H^{26}(M_{6,5};Q) vanishes, and no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26 when fibre cohomology is confined to q=0,1. [evidence: source; FND-0036, mechanically verified for degree 26.]
- The reduced-distinct-support locus in a degree-six relative linear system is open, and ordering its six support points gives a finite etale S_6-cover. [evidence: source; The canonical geometric bottleneck explicitly specifies the reduced-support open and its finite etale S_6-cover.]

## Candidate ideas requiring proof

- Identify W_5 with omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D) for a divisor D in a balanced tetragonal g^1_4, thereby interpreting the marked divisor as residual to D in a canonical divisor.
- Construct the rank-drop locus over the moduli of balanced tetragonal structures as the reduced-support open of the relative linear system |W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}|, followed by the finite etale ordering cover.
- Stratify the relative degree-six linear system by h^0(W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}) and determine every stratum's components, dimensions, stabilizers, and map to tetragonal moduli.
- For a free tetragonal pencil D with h^0(O_C(D))=2, Riemann-Roch suggests h^0(omega_C(-D))=3 and hence a P^2-family of residual degree-six divisors.
- Use localization and Gysin maps to isolate the exact contributions of the rank-drop locus to Gr^W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q).
- Reduce the lowest-weight cohomology of all relevant strata and coefficient systems to explicitly controlled configuration or Hurwitz spaces.
- Prove that every exact codimension-13 contribution supported on the rank-drop locus is a sum of Q(-13).

## Mathematical constraints

- M_{0,b} has cohomology only in even degrees. [reason: Already M_{0,4} is P^1 minus three points and has nonzero H^1; mixed-Tate cohomology does not imply concentration in even degrees.]
- An arbitrary finite etale cover of a space with pure-Tate cohomology also has pure-Tate cohomology. [reason: Transfer makes the base cohomology a direct summand of the cover's cohomology, not conversely; the cover may acquire additional non-Tate summands.]
- Being finite over an open subset of M_{0,b} is sufficient to make every lowest-weight cohomology group of a Hurwitz space Tate. [reason: Finiteness alone gives no such control on the new cohomology or monodromy of the covering space.]
- The h^0-stratification of a degree-six line bundle L with chi(L)=1 can contain an r=0 stratum. [reason: Riemann-Roch gives h^0(L)-h^1(L)=1, hence h^0(L)=1+h^1(L) is at least one.]
- Every non-Tate geometric variation necessarily has weight at least one. [reason: Non-Tate variations of weight zero can occur; finite-monodromy weight-zero systems must be analyzed separately rather than excluded by a positive-weight estimate.]
- The existence of a non-Tate local system on a stratum would by itself produce a surviving non-Tate summand after a Gysin map. [reason: A Gysin map may vanish or kill the relevant class, and survival in the exact degree and weight requires an explicit nonzero class and control of all differentials and boundary maps.]
- The absence of the f=4 obstruction proves that the f=5 residual condition is the unique global source of the target cohomology. [reason: The degree computation controls only the specified summands in the stated tetragonal construction; it does not exclude other geometric strata or coefficient systems without an exhaustive argument.]

## Reusable computations

- d=3g-3+n=3*6-3+6=21; 2d-16=26. [sha256: 0d488e15c0bfaa0097a55f1e288d020858517518b8c5bf48dbeff03d72b6d12b]
- deg(W_5)=4*6+12-4*5=16; deg(W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1})=16-(2*6-2)=6. [sha256: 6f4294cbc7166beabebcf00a625753ea71d2e5e71e458ad128f6458235bc972b]
- deg(omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma))=4*5+6-2*6-14=0; for f=4 it is 4*4+6-2*6-14=-4. [sha256: 0a749db765a4f0dbac4708d2dd3de1e406f25c54511d5cc9a8d72a152d0a049e]
- b=2g-2-4(-2)=18; dim(Hurwitz)=18-3=15; dim(Z)=15+2=17; codim(Z in M_{6,6})=21-17=4. [sha256: 7668e8f4ce20984ff651ab6440f19cfebc8af4bc5398f8e7d1c67de020cd7038]

## Dependencies to resolve

- A proof of the identification W_5 isomorphic to omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D), with the correct Casnati-Ekedahl convention and signs, is required.
- The balanced tetragonal moduli space, its components, dimension, splitting-type locus, and forgetful map to M_6 require rigorous construction and verification.
- Every h^0-stratum of the relative degree-six linear system requires a complete component and dimension analysis, including hyperelliptic, trigonal, nonreduced-support, and other special loci.
- The exact cohomology and monodromy of the relevant Hurwitz covers and finite ordering covers must be controlled; Tate cohomology cannot be inferred merely from finiteness over M_{0,b}.
- The Casnati-Ekedahl resolution must be shown to compute the exact lowest-weight degree-26 contribution on the complementary open locus.
- The localization or Gysin spectral sequence for the chosen stratification must be constructed with correct degree, weight, and Tate-twist conventions, and all relevant differentials must be controlled.
- Weight-zero nonconstant local systems and finite-monodromy representations on every contributing stratum require explicit analysis.
- Tate type for the exact codimension-13 contribution supported on the rank-drop locus remains to be proved.
- After controlling the supported contribution, its assembly with the complementary open contribution in Gr^W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) remains to be justified.
